WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
- Do you have any big plans
for Christmas this year?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.920
- Well, I'm going back to the
East Coast where my family is.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.770
I'm hoping for some snow
which would be really cool.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.710
It's a little weird to be in
California during the holidays.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.970
It's a little strange.
- I know. I'm not here either.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.803
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:12.803 --> 00:00:14.400
- I'm actually gonna be East Coast this-

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.540
- Are you?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.610
I love it. All snowy and stuff, yeah.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.810
- Me too. I hope we get some.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.240
- You're from somewhere magical
though, is it Burlington?

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.100
- I'm from Burlington, Massachusetts.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.240
- I've heard about Burlington,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.890
that it's like magical at Christmas time.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.510
- You did?
- I'm not kidding.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.800
I literally, I Google all the time

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.930
like, where's magical places
to go at Christmas time?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.160
And I swear to you, that comes up.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.630
- From Burlington, Massachusetts?

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.770
- I swear to you, it's that-

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.180
- You sure it isn't Vermont?

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.470
- There's a place in Vermont.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.210
And there's this random
place in Washington.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.400
I swear, I Google random things.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.630
But Burlington has come up.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:43.854
It's a very beautiful

00:00:43.854 --> 00:00:44.687
small town.
- I'm actually going back.

00:00:44.687 --> 00:00:46.350
My brother lives in Sweden.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.600
His family is coming in
and we're all going back

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.940
to my childhood home to
spend Christmas together,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:51.773
which is awesome.

00:00:51.773 --> 00:00:53.160
- That's cool.
- Yeah. Really cool.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.090
And it's been a long time

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.770
since we've all been in the same house.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.150
And all the grandkids
are gonna stay there.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.730
And we all have, you
know, like inflatable beds

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.350
and everyone's sleeping in the basement.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.270
Really fun. It's gonna be so fun.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.860
- My kids, it's so funny
you just said that.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.930
My daughter was like,
"Mom, okay, so I went

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.010
to my friend Leah's house

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.660
and, like, she had this really cool thing.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.630
They like blew it up and then
it was in their living room.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.650
We got to sleep in their living room."

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.060
And I'm like, "I love that, like,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.520
I work my butt off to provide you with

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.410
the most amazing room possible.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.240
The most comfy mattress.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.130
And yet still you want my childhood

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.200
of a blow up mattress from Walmart."

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.240
- 100%. That's all they want.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.377
- They do. They love it.

00:01:28.377 --> 00:01:29.283
And I love that vibe though.

00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:31.470
Like, there's so many people in the house.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.490
So I love that.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.448
I think that's cool.
- Yes, nobody in, nobody out.

00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:35.718
That's what we say. (laughs)

00:01:35.718 --> 00:01:37.770
- It's prison. It's forced family fun.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:38.940
It's a good time.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.160
Is there anything that annoys
you about the holiday time?

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.410
- Ooh, well I think that,

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.450
you know what I think is so cool now is

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.400
that everybody celebrates
it their own way.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.013
And I kind of feel,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.360
you know what annoys me, is
when people don't stop working

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.193
actually.
- Oh.

00:01:55.193 --> 00:01:57.180
- Like, I feel like when people assume

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.210
that you're gonna be
available all the time.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.980
You need to chill.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.280
If this young generation has
taught us anything, it's like,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.760
take a minute, allow yourself a day off.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:09.593
Whatever it is.
- This generation is like

00:02:09.593 --> 00:02:10.833
a walking Calm app.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.860
Yeah, they're really great about it.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.690
- They're like, work smarter, not harder.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.153
Productivity is a myth
that you've been sold.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.270
And we're like, no? Okay, yes.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.280
- Do you usually have a cutoff date? I do.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.080
Where I'm like I will
not do anything past,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.640
it's either when "The Voice" ends,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.650
that last day, the finale, I'm like, nope.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.510
- Same. We all have the same
"Voice" cutoff. (laughs)

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.120
- No, well, it's either
like, whatever show I'm doing

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.595
or this show, like we're done.

00:02:34.595 --> 00:02:36.750
Like this year it's
the 16th of December is

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.730
my first day out and I
will not work after it.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.430
So just so you know, everyone out there,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.510
I'm not doing anything.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.343
- That's really good.

00:02:43.343 --> 00:02:44.176
Yeah, no email.

00:02:44.176 --> 00:02:46.020
You have to like actually unplug.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.853
You have to unplug.

00:02:46.853 --> 00:02:48.600
So when people don't
do that, it stresses me

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.540
out a little bit, also because
I feel like I should be,

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.280
it's, you know-
- Yeah, don't make me feel bad

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.737
'cause you're still doing it.
- Don't make me feel bad.

00:02:54.737 --> 00:02:56.820
- Don't make me feel bad.
- Don't shame me 'cause I

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.690
need some time.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.970
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Okay, so wait. You cook.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.170
I know you're crafty.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.240
So is there any one skill,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.170
you're crafty.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.340
So you do all those kind of things.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.870
So is there any one skill
that you wish you had

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.670
that you don't have?
- Oh, so many.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.820
I mean, singing. I wish I
could play an instrument.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.653
You know what?

00:03:12.653 --> 00:03:13.530
I wish I could just go
into someone's house

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.660
at a party and be like, "Where
did you get this piano?"

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.250
Like, that would be my dream.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.840
- That's mine.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.770
- You cannot play the piano?

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.510
- I can play chords and, like,

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.557
write a song.
- Oh, only chords?

00:03:22.557 --> 00:03:24.813
- No, no, no, no. Ask Jason.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.060
- All you need is a little tinkle, like,

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.200
just like ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.197
And then someone comes over and goes,

00:03:29.197 --> 00:03:30.030
"What are you playing?"

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.320
Like, that's my dream.
- Yeah.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.000
- And I'd also like,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.310
I guess like rescuing someone
in front of a lot of people.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.360
That's what I would like to do.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.440
- Okay.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.120
You wanna be admired for being a hero?

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.160
- Yeah, just jumping in the
water and pulling someone

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.626
out and being like, "That's
just another day at work."

00:03:44.626 --> 00:03:45.690
And then you just get on the piano

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.860
and you just play a song that you-

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.900
- You do all of them combined.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.830
Oh, that house? I just built that.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.110
- And then you just jump
on your speedboat and you-

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:55.380
- We need this ad (laughs)
to go with this segment.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.330
- Wow, you're really
stumping me with skills.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.760
I know there's so many
of I would love to do.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.170
- I love that that answer though

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.800
because I feel like that's when
you really, like, are jaded.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.630
I feel like I love to keep learning.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.743
I love to learn new things.

00:04:07.743 --> 00:04:08.576
- Me too.
- I think it's fun.

00:04:08.576 --> 00:04:09.450
- Me too.
- Even if I'm not great at it.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.220
- I know and it's kind
of hard 'cause you're,

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.450
like, there's science behind it.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.820
Like your brain as it gets older gets,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.290
it gets harder to learn new things,

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.190
but it's what you're supposed to

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.900
do to keep your brain elastic.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.040
You know, you're supposed
to wear your watch

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.110
on the other side of your wrist
and you're supposed to brush

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.230
with the different hand just
to keep your brain moving.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.220
- I didn't know that.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.330
- Yeah. Do it tonight.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.640
- Oh my god, it's gonna feel
so weird with my left hand.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.690
- It'll feel so weird.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.630
And your brain grows
five times, I don't know.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.850
- I am ADHD though, so
I probably naturally do

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:36.683
a lot of these things.

00:04:36.683 --> 00:04:37.516
- Yeah, you probably do it anyway.

00:04:37.516 --> 00:04:38.733
- [Kelly] I'm like very weird.

